From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Render the ICC profiles with a host cd-create-profile

data/profiles renders the standard display profiles - sRGB, AdobeRGB,
Rec709 and the rest - by running the cd-create-profile that was just
built for the target, so meson stops at configure time:

    ERROR: An exe_wrapper is needed for .../client/cd-create-profile but
    was not found. Please define one in cross file and check the
    command and/or add it to PATH.

Unlike the reference spectra in data/cmf and data/illuminant, these
cannot simply be skipped: they install to /usr/share/color/icc/colord,
which the daemon scans at start-up and which is what the colour panel in
Settings lists, so an image without them has an empty panel.

The generator itself is small: cd-create-profile links the colour, DOM
and ICC halves of the library plus gio and lcms2, none of it hardware,
so a build machine copy is cheap to make. Add a host_cd_create_profile
option naming one; when set, the custom targets run it instead of the
target binary. A native build leaves it empty and behaves as before.

The host copy is compiled out of this same tree after configure - the
sources include config.h - so it does not exist yet when meson reads
this file. meson validates the first element of a custom_target command
at configure time whatever form it takes, string included:

    ERROR: Program '.../host-bin/cd-create-profile' not found or not
    executable

but the arguments after it are stored verbatim. So the shell goes first,
which always exists, and the generator's path is passed to it as $0 -
resolved only when ninja runs the command, by which time it is there.
@INPUT@ and @OUTPUT@ substitute across the whole command, so they work
from any position.

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -16,3 +16,4 @@
 option('pnp_ids', type : 'string', value : '', description : 'Location of pnp.ids if hwdb is not available')
 option('man', type : 'boolean', value : true, description : 'Generate man pages')
 option('docs', type : 'boolean', value : true, description : 'Generate documentation')
+option('host_cd_create_profile', type : 'string', value : '', description : 'Path to a cd-create-profile that runs on the build machine, for rendering the ICC profiles when cross compiling')
--- a/data/profiles/meson.build
+++ b/data/profiles/meson.build
@@ -47,6 +47,26 @@
   icc_profiles += icc_print_profiles
 endif
 
+# The cd-create-profile built above is for the target, so a cross build
+# cannot run it to render these:
+#
+#   ERROR: An exe_wrapper is needed for .../client/cd-create-profile but
+#   was not found.
+#
+# The generator only needs the colour and ICC halves of the library plus
+# gio and lcms2, none of it hardware, so a build machine copy is cheap.
+# It is compiled from this tree after configure, using config.h, so it
+# does not exist yet when this file is read. meson validates the first
+# element of a command at configure time whatever its type, but the
+# arguments after it are stored as-is, so the shell goes first and the
+# generator's path is handed to it as $0 - checked only when ninja runs.
+host_cd_create_profile = get_option('host_cd_create_profile')
+if host_cd_create_profile != ''
+  icc_generator = [ find_program('sh'), '-c', 'exec "$0" "$@"', host_cd_create_profile ]
+else
+  icc_generator = [ cd_create_profile ]
+endif
+
 generated_iccs = []
 foreach arg: icc_profiles
   xml_i18n = i18n.merge_file(
@@ -59,7 +79,7 @@
   generated_icc = custom_target(arg + '.icc',
     input: xml_i18n,
     output: arg + '.icc',
-    command: [ cd_create_profile, '--output=@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@' ],
+    command: icc_generator + [ '--output=@OUTPUT@', '@INPUT@' ],
     install: true,
     install_dir: join_paths(datadir, 'color', 'icc', 'colord'),
   )
